{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"FDA's device registry (GUDID) lists no NovaSeq X Dx or X Plus Dx device for Illumina, so regulated clinical labs still have no IVD-labelled X to move to.","detail":"I paged the AccessGUDID search 'NovaSeq 6000Dx Illumina' on 12 Oct 2026. It returned 53 results, and I read pages 1-6. No brand name contains 'NovaSeq X' or 'X Plus'. The only NovaSeq-branded Illumina Dx records are 6000Dx records. A separate search for 'NovaSeq X' matched only unrelated words ('Factor X', 'Fragile X'). A registry gap is not proof that nothing is pending at FDA, but it fits the known absence of an X IVD support page.","url":"https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/devices/search?query=NovaSeq+6000Dx+Illumina","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"FDA/NLM AccessGUDID","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"First registry-level check of GUDID for an X Dx device identifier (DI); prior notes covered only the Illumina support-page absence."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"All eight Illumina NovaSeq 6000Dx device records are still 'In Commercial Distribution' in GUDID, with no end date and no discontinuation notice.","detail":"The eight records are the instrument (00816270020637, model 20068232), Library Tube (…552), Library Tube 24-pack (…583), S2 and S4 v1.5 300-cycle reagent kits (…538, …569), S2 and S4 buffer cartridges (…545, …576), and the DRAGEN DNA Prep with Enrichment Dx app (…743, model 20074609). All show status 'In Commercial Distribution'. The lookups I ran for the instrument, library tube and DRAGEN app returned a null end date. I did not run lookups for the other five. The registry shows no wind-down of the regulated 6000 line.","url":"https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/devices/00816270020637","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"FDA/NLM AccessGUDID","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Adds the official registry status of the 6000Dx kit set; the known list had only the Illumina web pages and package inserts."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The 6000Dx device records are frozen at their Oct-Nov 2022 launch versions, with no later versions.","detail":"The instrument and the Library Tube both have a device publish date of 18 Oct 2022 and a public version 1 dated 26 Oct 2022 ('New'), with no later versions. The DRAGEN 6000Dx app was published 7 Nov 2022, also version 1. Nearly four years without a record update fits the known unchanged package inserts and the 26-month gap in 6000Dx software releases. The regulated tail has no refresh and no successor.","url":"https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/api/v3/devices/lookup.json?di=00816270020637","date":"2022-10-26","source_name":"FDA/NLM AccessGUDID API","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Gives registry version dates, which are not in the known package-insert and software-release evidence."},
